# UI copy

User-facing strings are brief, professional, and essential only. Same bar for checkboxes, headings, alerts, help, helper text, and tooltips.

- One idea per string. Prefer a clause over a paragraph.
- Checkboxes name the commitment. Do not list other screens or “you can still edit.”
- Page descriptions: what the screen is. Do not narrate the workflow.
- Empty project: `Select a project.`
- Below tablet width: `Desktop required` / `Peggy is built for desktop web.`
- Tooltips: a few words, not a sentence with “and.”
- Help: facts and locations, not a tour. Prefer an (i) `InfoTip` next to the heading, not a paragraph under it. Dashboard keeps visible body copy.
- Table row actions use icons (`aria-label`). Exceptions: Reading journal, Calendar, Ethics, Methods plan.
- Privacy/consent: keep the legal fact; drop the rest.

Do not use: “I’m happy with…”, “for now”, “You can still…”, “Click to…”, “Sample data shown” unless the UI is actually sample data.